Backend notes:
<!-- npm init -y -->
creates package.json(maintains dependencies and scripts)
<!-- npm install express pg dotenv cors -->
These four packages have clear purposes:
express-Creates our REST API/server
pg-Connects Node.js to PostgreSQL
dotenv-Reads secrets/configuration from .env
cors-Allows your React frontend to communicate with the backend
<!-- backend/.env -->

- The separate backend/ folder keeps the new PostgreSQL API apart from the old SQLite server.js.
- backend/package.json lists the packages used by the backend and its start commands.
- Express creates the web server; CORS lets the frontend make requests to it.
- express.json() lets Express read JSON request bodies.
- backend/.env stores local settings like the port and database login; never share its password.
- backend/.gitignore keeps .env and node_modules out of Git.
- backend/config/db.js uses a PostgreSQL Pool to reuse database connections.
- backend/server.js starts the API and defines GET /api/health as a connection check.
- npm run dev starts the backend and restarts it when server files change.
- npm start starts the backend without watching for file changes.

